<title>UK: Forcados delayed 2-3 days, no cancellations yet-NN.</title>
<headline>Forcados delayed 2-3 days, no cancellations yet-NN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Force majeure on Nigerian Forcados liftings following community disturbances had delayed loadings by two to three days but no cargoes had so far been cancelled, a Nigerian National Petroleum Corp official said on Friday.  </p>
<p>Forcados operator Royal Dutch Shell said ethnic clashes had forced it to close 20 percent of its Forcados production.</p>
<p>Traders said the shut-in amounted to about 90,000 barrels a day (bpd) of the 450,000 bpd stream.</p>
<p>The NNPC official said Forcados cargoes scheduled to load from April 29 to May 6 had been put back by two days. Lifters of Forcados loading from May 7-20 had been informed of a three-day delay, he added.</p>
</text>
